2026-10-31T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Bao unseals itself through a Seal Bao on Fly
 # uuid: cbb5a188-fb11-5d9f-b46f-da4fc30e08c6
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l2, rfd:attest-in:details
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-10-31T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2354) 'the seal of every Bao, its key, and its recovery.
 # tags: rfd:scope
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Bao restarts and unseals with no person at the keyboard.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Three Baos mean three seal states and three unseal calls per fleet restart.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Pass the recovery test on clean hosts before prod moves; the sections below hold the steps.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Bao unseals itself through a Seal Bao on Fly
 # tags: rfd:details-title
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2354) 'A transit seal on a Seal Bao on Fly, unwrapped from Fly KMS at boot (operator,
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2354) '2026-10-30). Recovery becomes hands-off, not operator-with-1P. Superseded on 2026-11-01:
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Bao runs as one Fly machine and unseals from Fly KMS at boot, with an offline division of
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2354) 'the seal key with n=1 as the last resort (operator, 2026-11-01).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2354) 'RFD66606-2144, RFD66606-2145, RFD66606-2146.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Split from the old RFD66606-2147: RFD66606-2353 (replicas), 2355 (cache), 2356 (no CDN proxy).
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Auto-unseal: KMS wrapper, Shamir stays as break-glass
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Shamir with a manual share is the right seal for one-of-one, wrong for
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2354) 'three-of-three. Options:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2354) '- **Cloud KMS seal** (AWS KMS, GCP KMS, Azure Key Vault, Oracle). The
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2354) '  key stays in the cloud KMS; Bao decrypts the master key at boot via
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2354) '  the KMS API. Standard pattern. Cost is per-request against the KMS,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2354) '  measured in fractions of a cent per unseal.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2354) '- **Transit seal** (a second, seed-only Bao). Chicken-and-egg unless
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2354) '  the seed Bao is truly offline (Raspberry Pi, HSM, boot-from-USB).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2354) '  Adds a second thing to maintain.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2354) '- **HSM / PKCS#11**. Right answer for a fleet in a datacenter with
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2354) '  its own HSM. Overkill for this workspace's scale.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2354) '- **HCP Vault / OpenBao managed**. Not this workspace's shape.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Recommendation: Fly KMS, through a Seal Bao. Fly app secret keys are a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2354) 'first-party KMS, usable only from inside a machine of the owning app, and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2354) 'OpenBao has no Fly seal type, so a Seal Bao bridges the two (operator,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2354) '2026-10-30). The break-glass key for the day the KMS itself is the outage
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2354) '(the day RFD66606-2144 logs as its eleventh defect) is the Seal Bao's static key, held offline
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2354) 'as a Shamir share, whose count may be 1.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2354) 'An auto-unseal wrapper does not change the CRL-loop bug logged
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2354) 'during the DR (Bao's authenticated paths going flaky after a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2354) 'particular sequence of issuer imports). That is a separate item.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Transit seal on Fly, unwrapped by Fly KMS
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2354) 'The operator chose on 2026-10-13 to unseal the Fly instances from a small Bao,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2354) 'rescinded the Mac mini as its host on 2026-10-30, and chose a Seal Bao on Fly that
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2354) 'unwraps its own key from Fly KMS (operator, 2026-10-30).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2354) '- Encrypt and decrypt with a Fly secret key work only from inside a machine of the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2354) '  owning app, through the machine's local API socket; the public API refuses. The Seal
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2354) '  Bao's start-up script decrypts a wrapped 32-byte key into memory and starts Bao with a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2354) '  `static` seal. Every other Bao uses a stock transit seal against it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2354) '- The Seal Bao runs as one machine or as an HA set of three voters. Two voters tolerate
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2354) '  no failure, so two is not a valid setting (operator, 2026-10-30). One machine relies on
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2354) '  a restore from backup that has been tested.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2354) '- It listens only on its tailnet address, over TLS, and the tailnet policy lets only Bao
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2354) '  nodes reach it. No peer reaches a localhost or public listener.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2354) '- Each Bao has its own transit key and a policy limited to encrypt and decrypt on that
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2354) '  key. A certificate login yields a short token, but a seal needs its token at boot, so
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2354) '  each Bao also holds a periodic orphan token for its key: a Fly secret on the Fly
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2354) '  instances, a file readable only by its own user elsewhere. Measured on a throwaway Bao,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2354) '  the seal renews that token while the Bao runs; the token expires if the Bao is down
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2354) '  longer than its period, so the period is set to days and a longer outage needs a new
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2354) '  token.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2354) '- If the Seal Bao is down, a restarted Bao stays sealed until it is back. Running Baos
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2354) '  keep serving.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2354) '- The break-glass key is the Seal Bao's static key, held offline as a Shamir share even
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2354) '  when the count is 1, and never in the backup bucket. A new Seal Bao started with that
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2354) '  key and a restored snapshot unlocks every other Bao. Each Bao's Shamir recovery keys
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2354) '  authorise operations such as generating a root token; they do not unseal.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2354) '- The Seal Bao backs up to the same bucket as the others, under its own prefix, with
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2354) '  unique object names and a retention lock; plain-text config files stay out of the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2354) '  snapshots and are protected separately.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2354) '- The change is proved with a planted control: with the Seal Bao stopped, a restarted
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-2354) '  Bao stays sealed. The recovery test passes before prod moves: on clean hosts with Fly
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-2354) '  blocked, restore the Seal Bao from the offline key and the backup, then restore one
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-2354) '  other Bao through it and read back data.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Recovery without Fly KMS
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-2354) 'This procedure needs no Fly account, no Fly machine and no network path to Fly. It is
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-2354) 'the one the recovery test runs (operator, 2026-10-30).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-2354) '1. Gather the materials: the offline Shamir share or shares of the Seal Bao's static
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-2354) '   key, the Seal Bao's configuration without its secrets, and the newest snapshot of
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-2354) '   the Seal Bao from the backup bucket.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2354) '2. Rebuild the key: combine the shares into the 32-byte key (one share is the key
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2354) '   itself). Check the length and the key id the configuration names before use.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2354) '3. Start a new Seal Bao on any host with a `static` seal whose key is a file in memory
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2354) '   backed storage, and with the same listener rules: tailnet address, TLS.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2354) '4. Restore the snapshot into it. Whether the restore needs the force option under a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2354) '   fresh barrier is not yet measured; the recovery test settles it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2354) '5. Check that the transit keys, the policies and the cert roles are back, and that one
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-2354) '   other Bao unseals through the new address with its existing periodic token.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:33Z (RFD66606-2354) '6. Point the other Baos at the new address if it changed, one at a time.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:34Z (RFD66606-2354) '7. Resume hands-off unsealing by wrapping the key with a new KMS, or by leaving it
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:35Z (RFD66606-2354) '   manual until one exists. A Bao that stays up needs none of this; only a restart does.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:36Z (RFD66606-2354) '8. Write down what the restore took and which step was unclear, then amend this block.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:37Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:38Z (RFD66606-2354) 'The key never leaves the offline store except during steps 2 and 3, and the memory copy
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:39Z (RFD66606-2354) 'is destroyed when the host stops.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:40Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:41Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Alternative wrapper: a passkey
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:42Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Fly KMS is the hands-off wrapper. A passkey can wrap the same 32-byte static key when no
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:43Z (RFD66606-2354) 'Fly KMS is available, at the price of a person at every restart (operator, 2026-10-30).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:44Z (RFD66606-2354) 'The route has not been run here; the recovery test measures it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:45Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:46Z (RFD66606-2354) '- **Passkey.** A passkey whose authenticator offers a secret-derivation extension can
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:47Z (RFD66606-2354) '  derive a wrapping key from a challenge, with a touch. Support differs by authenticator
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:48Z (RFD66606-2354) '  and by client library, so confirm that the same credential returns the same secret on
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:49Z (RFD66606-2354) '  a second host before relying on it. A passkey that only signs cannot wrap anything.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:50Z (RFD66606-2354) '- **Hardware seal in Bao.** OpenBao can seal through a PKCS#11 module, but that needs a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:51Z (RFD66606-2354) '  token that decrypts or unwraps with a mechanism the seal supports; whether a passkey
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:52Z (RFD66606-2354) '  does is not known. Until measured, the passkey wraps the static key and Bao keeps its
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:53Z (RFD66606-2354) '  `static` seal.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:54Z (RFD66606-2354) '- Keep two passkeys, stored apart, since one lost token otherwise ends recovery. A
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:55Z (RFD66606-2354) '  passkey stays out of the backup bucket and off any Fly host.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:56Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:57Z (RFD66606-2354) 'How the key arrives, and rotating the seal
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:58Z (RFD66606-2354) 'A Bao on a `static` seal holds one 32-byte key. How that key reaches the process is a
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:01:59Z (RFD66606-2354) 'mode in the start-up script, not part of the seal. Every mode supplies the same key, so
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:00Z (RFD66606-2354) 'a node changes mode with no migration (operator, 2026-10-30).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:01Z (RFD66606-2354) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:02Z (RFD66606-2354) '- `tpm`: a non-exportable TPM key unwraps a wrapped copy of the key at start, with no
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

