 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:05Z (RFD66606-2354) '  the key.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:06Z (RFD66606-2354) '- `passkey`: a person touches the passkey at each start.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:07Z (RFD66606-2354) '- `manual`: the script asks a person for the key, for example from the offline Shamir
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:08Z (RFD66606-2354) '  shares, and then starts Bao. Bao does not start without the key, and a `static` seal
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:09Z (RFD66606-2354) '  has no manual unseal of its own. A node left in this mode starts nothing on its own.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:10Z (RFD66606-2354) '- A node lists the modes it has in order and uses the first that works, for example
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:11Z (RFD66606-2354) '  `tpm`, then `kms`, then `passkey`, then `manual`. Each node wraps the key once per
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:12Z (RFD66606-2354) '  mode it lists, so any one is enough (operator, 2026-10-30). The script logs which mode
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:13Z (RFD66606-2354) '  unwrapped the key, so a fallback shows. Splitting the key so that several modes are all
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:02:14Z (RFD66606-2354) '  required is not used: one broken mode would then block the start.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2354  1 LINE
 Text:Written

